{"t": 1794112736.1837735, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found\n\nCause: the upstream ledger (2026.11) started including a `currency` field on every row. `reports/export.py` built its CSV writer with a hardcoded fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\"], so `csv.DictWriter` raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` on every export request, crashing the export handler (502).\n\nEvidence: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1), 2026-11-04 19:02:11 \u2014 `ERROR export failed: ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` next to `INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row`.\n\nFix: `reports/export.py` now derives the CSV columns from the row keys (id, amount, plus any extra fields such as currency) instead of hardcoding them. Verified against rows with and without `currency`; output is unchanged for the old schema. Needs deploy + a re-check of the export endpoint.\n\nNo incident was open in Grafana and no Sentry project exists for reports-api, so this note is the only record \u2014 please confirm the deploy and close out."}, "ok": true}
